  "flags": [
    {
      "page": 3,
      "what": "The skill table's ticks are glyphs the text layer drops: the table was read from p3's image. The Pirate column is ticked for the Captain, the Mate and the Cabin Boy."
    },
    {
      "page": 3,
      "what": "The Swabbie Equipment list's Missile Weapons (Belaying Pin 3 gc, Bow 10 gc) and Armour (Buckler 5 gc, Toughened leathers 5 gc) are printed at the top of the right column, continuing the left column; read that way, as the Araby Smugglers' and Slayer Pirates' pages are laid out the same."
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "what": "A Pirate warband needs at least 3 models: our templates hold no minimum, so it is not imported. No henchmen group sizes and no maximum profile are printed: the crew takes our Human race."
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "what": "Swabbies have no hire price (they are captured, not hired): their cost is 0 gc."
    },
    {
      "page": 3,
      "what": "The Swivel Gun's line is 65 gc, Rare 8, one per warband; our Swivel Gun is 65 gc, Rare 8 already, so the line only carries the limit."
    },
    {
      "page": 3,
      "what": "The Cat O' Nine Tails, Boat Hook, Belaying Pin, Swivel Gun and its Ball, Chain and Grape Shot are all ours, at the list's prices; the PDF prints no rules for them."
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "what": "\"at warband creation, you may purchase dueling pistols for 25gc each\": list prices are starting prices in the app, so the Duelling Pistol's line is 25 gc (50 for a brace) and no rule repeats it."
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "what": "The rule names \"a Bretonnian hero\", so the short-range change is written for Heroes only, as printed."
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "what": "The Pirate column is the Pirate Skills list of the Sartosa campaign rules (Sartosa Skills, Hired Swords and Dramatis Personae, p1-2), not this PDF: it is the shared Sartosa Pirate Skills group, declared in sartosan-pirates.json and named by each hero who ticks it."
    }
  ]
